@flexiarg problems/snatch-play-theory-gaps
@title Problem node: Snatch institutions need a theory of play, not only defence
@keywords problem-node, section-grain, snatch, institutions, play-theory, gaps
@audience futon stack operators, library authors
@tone plain
@style pattern
@why section-doc authority: futon3 library/snatch/README.md, "Not yet a complete theory of play" and "The gaps filled, and reviewed" sections (quoted with pointers below; no library pattern grounds this node)
@how no mechanism claimed at problem grain; the section's patterns are the mechanisms -- design-grain entries mapped to treatments G1-G5 in the README's Six patterns table, play-grain entries written against the six named gaps

! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node at section grain for the snatch section: the README itself assessed the collection as "Not yet a complete theory of play" with six named gaps, and then recorded the gaps being filled -- the section's patterns exist to answer that assessed problem and the syllogism test (Alexander patterns ~= Ostrom institutions ~= policies) the section was commissioned for.

  + context: Minted by library-loop row L18 v2 after review found the blanket no-source claim false for 19 refused snatch/* patterns. Source: futon3 library/snatch/README.md.

  + IF:
    A library section is read as institutions-for-play and consulted by a served cascade (snatch-cascade consults 12 of its members).

  + HOWEVER:
    The section's own assessment states the problem: "Not yet a complete theory of play ... Eleven patterns: six design-grain, five play-grain. Six gaps, the first structural and the rest missing entries" -- gap 1 "Nothing states the gain -- every pattern is defensive", gap 2 "P2 has no patterns at all", gap 3 "The ask is unaddressed", gap 4 "G2 and G5 have no play patterns", gap 5 "The horizon is ignored", gap 6 "No re-entry condition" (source: library/snatch/README.md, "Not yet a complete theory of play" section). The follow-up record states the repair: "codex-22 wrote seven play-grain patterns against the six gaps above (550d4786)" with per-gap closure and three review fixes (source: same README, "The gaps filled, and reviewed" section).

  + THEN:
    This node is the landing point for the shared @why edges from the snatch patterns (mechanical pass, row L18 v2): the design-grain six are mapped to treatments G1-G5 in the README's Six patterns table, and the gap-filled play patterns are named in the gaps-filled record; per-pattern questions route to that record, not to invention here.

  + BECAUSE:
    A section whose own README names the problem each cohort of patterns was written against carries one problem node, not per-pattern copies (the L11/L15/L18 cost finding).

    + evidence: futon3 library/snatch/README.md -- "Not yet a complete theory of play" (six gaps), "The gaps filled, and reviewed" (550d4786), and the Six patterns treatment table; L17/L18 advisory reports.
